Grove PATCH-21: make BCH electrum select BitcoinCash servers, and configurable

PATCH-18 added thirteen live-verified "bitcoincash" entries to
DEFAULT_ELECTRUM_SERVERS and wired BCHInterface to _initElectrumBackend. It
did not add BCH to the one map that decides WHICH server set a backend uses,
so those entries were dead data that nothing ever selected.

  wallet_backend.py
      ElectrumBackend.__init__'s coin_name_map held only BTC and LTC and fell
      through to "bitcoin" for anything else. coin_name is the sole input to
      ElectrumServer's DEFAULT_ELECTRUM_SERVERS lookup, so a BCH client built
      on the default path -- basicswap-prepare --light or --bch-mode=electrum,
      neither of which writes electrum_clearnet_servers -- connected to
      BITCOIN's servers and answered every balance, UTXO, height and fee query
      from the wrong chain, with broadcasts rejected. Silently: the .get()
      default never warned, and the log line reads
      "ElectrumServer bitcoin: 6 clearnet servers", which looks entirely
      normal.

      Proven by construction, not inferred -- building the object with exactly
      the arguments _initElectrumBackend passes gives
          BTC -> bitcoin | LTC -> litecoin | BCH -> bitcoin
      An unmapped coin now RAISES instead of defaulting. A wrong-chain default
      is strictly worse than a startup failure: it is silent, and it presents
      as an empty wallet. Note line 174 of the same constructor already used a
      generic chainparams.get(coin_type, ...) -- one lookup in this function
      was generic and the one immediately below it was hardcoded.

      Why every earlier gate missed it: the one live run used a regtest
      Fulcrum via an explicit --bch-electrum-server, i.e. the single
      configuration where user-supplied servers are set and coin_name is
      irrelevant. The server-list check verified the bitcoincash entries'
      CONTENTS and REACHABILITY, never that anything SELECTS them.

  ui/page_settings.py, js_server.py
      Three more copies of the same allowlist -- the settings POST handler,
      the settings render path, and the JSON endpoint -- each listing only
      bitcoin and litecoin. BCH could run in electrum mode but could not be
      configured from the UI, and the endpoint refused to return servers for a
      coin the backend genuinely supports.

This is why the missing map mattered so much for BCH specifically: Fulcrum is
deliberately NOT bundled (it is harness-only), so for BCH light mode the
public bitcoincash server list IS the backend, and coin_name_map was the only
thing standing between the user and it.

Kept separate from PATCH-20 so it stays exportable as an upstream-facing
change alongside PATCH-18 -- see scripts/swap/export-upstream-pr.mjs.

Applies on top of PATCH-20.

diff --git a/basicswap/wallet_backend.py b/basicswap/wallet_backend.py
index 89c6103..a6863e6 100644
--- a/basicswap/wallet_backend.py
+++ b/basicswap/wallet_backend.py
@@ -174,11 +174,31 @@ class ElectrumBackend(WalletBackend):
         coin_params = chainparams.get(coin_type, chainparams.get(Coins.BTC))
         self._network_params = coin_params.get(chain, coin_params.get("mainnet", {}))
 
+        # PWNDA-PATCH-21: BCH was missing here, and the default silently made it
+        # Bitcoin. coin_name is the ONLY thing that selects a server set --
+        # ElectrumServer looks it up in DEFAULT_ELECTRUM_SERVERS -- so a BCH client
+        # built on the default path (no --bch-electrum-server, hence
+        # clearnet_servers=None) connected to Bitcoin's servers and answered every
+        # balance, UTXO, height and fee query from the wrong chain, with broadcasts
+        # rejected and nothing logged out of the ordinary.
+        #
+        # Raise on an unmapped coin rather than defaulting. A wrong-chain default is
+        # strictly worse than a startup failure: it is silent, and it looks like an
+        # empty wallet. Note line 174 above already uses a generic
+        # chainparams.get(coin_type, ...) -- one lookup in this constructor was
+        # generic and the one immediately below it was hardcoded.
         coin_name_map = {
             Coins.BTC: "bitcoin",
             Coins.LTC: "litecoin",
+            Coins.BCH: "bitcoincash",
         }
-        coin_name = coin_name_map.get(coin_type, "bitcoin")
+        if coin_type not in coin_name_map:
+            raise ValueError(
+                f"ElectrumBackend has no server set for {coin_type}; add it to "
+                f"coin_name_map and to DEFAULT_ELECTRUM_SERVERS before enabling "
+                f"electrum mode for this coin"
+            )
+        coin_name = coin_name_map[coin_type]
 
         self._host = "localhost"
         self._port = 50002
